  "result": "I wrote the revised record to `record.jsonl`. Only the `blind` scenario changed.\n\n`blind` now masks `rel.occupies` instead of `rel.longitudinal_overlap`. Masking the overlap couldn't make the rule unknown: Core recomputes the overlap from position, heading and extent, and the adapter needs all three for any track whose lane occupancy is observed.\n\nWith lane occupancy masked, the overlap is still decided at 2 m. But whether the car is in the motorcycle's lane, and whether the motorcycle is on the highway, both become unknown, so the rule should report unknown on the masked atom. I worked this out from the coder's rule and haven't run it through the gate. The new narrative says the car and motorcycle are side by side and their lane and highway occupancy isn't observed.\n\nThe coder's rule itself needs no change. All the other scenarios passed the gate, and the rest of the record is as planned.",
